# Force LF for scripts that run on the Linux deploy target.
# CRLF in a shell script breaks the shebang (#!/bin/bash^M) and any
# here-doc / variable expansion, so these must stay LF regardless of
# core.autocrlf on the Windows build machine. The deploy tar.gz is
# built from the working tree, so a CRLF checkout would ship a broken
# script to Ubuntu.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
